{
  "brief_rationale": "The doctor established the right-eye postoperative episode and reconciled the left-eye prior history confusion by referencing discharge paperwork and the family’s own report. All serious safety duties (laterality, red-flag screening, eye-drop safety, preoperative-vs-discharge boundary, caregiver execution, follow-up handoff, non-overreach) were met without error. Two high-order points—co-designing a low-burden medication system for rotating caregivers (HO1) and bounded-closure reasoning that separates allowed from blocking risks (HO3)—were actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact. No important non-chain defect was found, so the trajectory meets all Strong requirements.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00150",
        "explanation": "Doctor provides a final closure statement confirming the plan is safe to execute until review, acknowledging residual monitoring and escalation paths.",
        "quote": "目前这个方案完全可以放心执行到一周后复查。"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The plan leaves the family with a clear, written medication schedule, a logging method, and an explicit follow-up owner and timing; the doctor’s final message confirms the plan as fully executable through the next review.",
    "label": "valid_closure",
    "safe": true,
    "traceable": true
  },
  "dimension_citations": {
    "actionability_responsibility_chain": [
